# Cell from playpick: mode=menus, view=844x390,touch, save=carried.
# direction.md's "Not yet filed" list has two items this session answers at
# once: "a real player's path through the front door is still mostly
# untested" (almost every session reaches a fight via an invite hash) and
# "convenience/tap-count findings are accumulating informally but not yet
# measured with `ui`". So: walk the real front page -> RAID -> setup ->
# class pick -> PULL chain, count every tap by hand against the journal, and
# run `ui` on each screen along the way, landscape phone / carried profile.
open
targets
ui
shot front

tap raid
targets
ui
shot raid-setup

tap next
targets
ui
shot class-pick

tap class:shaman:elemental
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrived
state

# front page -> raid -> class -> pull -> standing in the first room (the
# evening has begun; the entrance corridor is itself contested ground) took
# 4 taps. Now the way back out, and the battleground path for comparison.
key Escape
targets
shot after-escape
tap back
tap back
targets
shot back-to-front

tap battleground
targets
ui
shot bg-setup
tap map:conquest
targets
shot bg-class-pick
tap class:priest:discipline
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot bg-arrived
state
